.TH WATCH 1
.SH NAME
Watch \- run a command again each time a file is Put, in acme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Watch
[
.B -r
] [
.I cmd ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Watch
opens an
.IR acme (1)
window,
.IB dir /+watch\f1,
for the current directory
.IR dir ,
runs
.I cmd
there with
.IR rc (1),
and shows what it prints under a first line,
.BI % " cmd"\f1.
Each time a file in
.I dir
is written by
.I acme
(Put), it runs the command again, after stopping it if it is still running,
and its output replaces the last.
Several files written at once, as by
.BR Putall ,
make one run.
With
.BR -r ,
a file in a directory below
.I dir
counts too.
Without
.IR cmd ,
the command is
.BR mk .
.PP
The first line may be edited: the next run is what it says.
.B Get
in the window's tag runs it now,
.B Kill
stops it, and
.B Del
ends
.IR Watch .
A command that fails says so on a last line,
.BI "% exit " status\f1.
Button 3 on a
.IB file : line
in the output opens it, as anywhere in
.IR acme .
.PP
.I Watch
is Russ Cox's, from
.BR 9fans.net/go/acme/Watch ,
in Plan 9 C.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the tests whenever a source file is saved:
.IP
.EX
Watch mk test
.EE
.PP
Rebuild on devbox, over
.IR ssh (1),
when a file of its, mounted by
.IR sshfs (4),
is Put:
.IP
.EX
cd /n/devbox/home/dev/sd
Watch ssh devbox 'cd sd && cargo test -q'
.EE
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/Watch.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR acme (4)
.SH BUGS
Only Puts by
.I acme
count: a file changed by another program does not start a run.
